{
 "format": "pcbpro",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "Extreme high gain (5 stages) 100W",
 "author": "",
 "revision": "A",
 "notes": "Extreme high gain (5 stages) 100W\nHigh gain: saturated from low GAIN settings - lead and heavy rhythm.\n\nOutput: 4 x 6L6GC, push-pull class AB, fixed bias, adjustable\nOutput power: about 100 W clean into 8 ohm\nB+ / plate: 460 V at the OT, about 460 V plate to cathode\nIdle current: 36 mA per tube (bias about -50 V)\nPlate dissipation: 14.9 W per tube = 50% of the 30 W rating\nBias adjust range: -29 V to -58 V (fail-safe: an open trimmer gives maximum negative bias)\nPresence: up to +7 dB at 4 kHz (in the power amp, after the distortion)\nDepth: up to +6 dB at 80 Hz - low-end thump at the cabinet's resonance without loosening the preamp\n\nWhere it distorts (gain on 10): The distortion is spread over 4 stages (V1B, V2A, V2B, V3A): smooth, saturated and compressed.\n  V1A (input): clean\n  V1B (second stage): clips, +19 dB\n  V2A (cold clipper): clips, +27 dB\n  V2B (fourth stage): clips, +24 dB\n  V3A (fifth stage): clips, +22 dB\n  FXR (loop recovery): clean\nTightness tight: low E (6-string) -22 dB, low B (7-string) -26 dB, low F# (8-string) -31 dB (into the distortion, relative to 1 kHz)\nHiss with the gain on 10: about -18 dB below the playing level (-38 dB with the gain at noon)\n\nPedal: Noise gate (4-cable, for the effects loop) - in the effects loop, keyed from your guitar (4-cable method): silence between riffs without choking the notes\nPedal: Tight boost - in front of the input: tightens the low end and focuses the mids for palm mutes and solos\nPedal: High-gain distortion - a high-gain distortion pedal for a second voice, or into a clean amp\n\nPower transformer: 345-0-345 VAC at 479 mA DC, 6.3 V 7.3 A, bias tap about 55 VAC; 230 V primary, about 291 VA\nOutput transformer: 2k plate-to-plate to 8 ohm, 130 W or more\nFilter choke: 5-10 H, 32 mA or more\nMains fuse: T2.5 A slow-blow (230 V), plus a power switch\nTubes: 5 x 12AX7, 4 x 6L6GC\nRectifier: 4 x 1N4007 on the board (solid state)\nSpeaker: 8 ohm, 150 W or more\nChassis parts: 1/4\" speaker jack, power and (optional) standby switches, mains inlet, pilot lamp, knobs\n\n- Tightness 'tight': going into the distortion the low E (82 Hz) is 22 dB down on the mids, a 7-string's low B 26 dB and an 8-string's F# 31 dB. Fast palm mutes stay articulate; the DEPTH control puts the thump back in the power amp.\n- The heaters are elevated to about +52 V: the cathode follower's cathode sits near 200 V, and this keeps the heater-to-cathode voltage inside the 12AX7's rating (and lowers hum).\n- The 4 preamp tubes' heaters run on filtered DC (about 6.2 V, 1.2 A): no heater hum in the high-gain stages. Measure it with the tubes in: 6.0-6.6 V is right; change the 1R dropping resistor if it is outside that.\n- The 4 6L6GCs draw 3.6 A of heater current: run twisted pairs from the 6.3 V winding to each power tube's H1/H2 pads (or daisy-chain the pads) instead of wide board traces; the preamp tubes' heaters stay on the board.\n- Before the first power-up turn the BIAS trimmer for the most negative bias, then set it for about 32 mA per tube: 32 mV across each 1R cathode resistor (pads K1-K4).\n- If the amp squeals or motorboats when you turn it up, the feedback is positive: swap the two output-transformer secondary leads (SPK / COM).\n- Solid-state rectification gives a tight, punchy response with full B+ at switch-on; the filter caps are rated for the no-load voltage.\n- Mains wiring (inlet, fuse, switch, transformer primary) stays on the chassis. The board carries lethal voltages: the bleeder drains the caps in about a minute - always measure B+ before touching anything.\n- Hiss: with the gain on 10 the input stage's hiss comes within 18 dB of clipping V3A, so expect audible hiss between riffs - a noise gate in the effects loop (keyed from the guitar) is the standard cure - see Amp > Metal pedals.\n- Low noise: fit a low-noise (selected) 12AX7 as V1, use metal-film resistors in the first two stages, shielded wire to the input jack, and keep the heater and mains wiring twisted and away from V1/V2.\n- A tight boost in front (Tube Screamer style, drive at zero, level up) is the classic metal trick: it cuts the lows before the preamp and pushes the mids - the Tight Boost pedal in Amp > Metal pedals.\n- Cabinet: a closed-back 2x12 or 4x12 with Vintage 30 / G12K-100 class speakers; set DEPTH for the low-end thump of your cab and PRESENCE for the cut.\n- For the tightest low end bias the power tubes on the cool side (60-70 % of their plate rating) and use a solid-state rectifier - both are this design's defaults.\n\nFirst power-up:\n1. Check every electrolytic's polarity, the heater wiring and the mains wiring before the first switch-on, and bring the amp up through a dim-bulb tester or a variac.\n2. With no tubes fitted the heaters should read 6.3 VAC at the sockets and B+ will sit high (about 487 V): the filter caps are rated for it.\n3. Always connect a speaker (or a load resistor) before playing: an unloaded output transformer can arc and destroy the power tubes or itself.\n4. Fit the tubes with the BIAS trimmer at maximum negative bias, then set 32 mA per tube (32 mV across each 1R).\n5. Measure the B+ nodes and the tube pins against the tables below: within 10-15 % means the amp is healthy.\n\nVoltage chart (DC to ground at idle):\nV1 12AX7: 1 PA 161 V, 2 GA 0.0 V, 3 KA 1.1 V, 4 H 58.2 V, 5 H 58.2 V, 6 PB 181 V, 7 GB 0.0 V, 8 KB 1.4 V, 9 HCT 52 V\nV2 12AX7: 1 PA 238 V, 2 GA 0.0 V, 3 KA 2.1 V, 4 H 58.2 V, 5 H 58.2 V, 6 PB 202 V, 7 GB 0.0 V, 8 KB 1.6 V, 9 HCT 52 V\nV3 12AX7: 1 PA 225 V, 2 GA 0.0 V, 3 KA 1.7 V, 4 H 58.2 V, 5 H 58.2 V, 6 PB 290 V, 7 GB 225 V, 8 KB 226 V, 9 HCT 52 V\nV4 12AX7: 1 PA 317 V, 2 GA 0.0 V, 3 KA 2.4 V, 4 H 58.2 V, 5 H 58.2 V, 6 PB 246 V, 7 GB 0.0 V, 8 KB 1.9 V, 9 HCT 52 V\nV5 12AX7: 1 PA 306 V, 2 GA 24 V, 3 KA 25 V, 4 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 5 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 6 PB 284 V, 7 GB 24 V, 8 KB 25 V, 9 HCT 6.3 VAC on +52 V\nV6 6L6GC: 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 455 V, 5 G1 -50 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V\nV7 6L6GC: 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 455 V, 5 G1 -50 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V\nV8 6L6GC: 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 455 V, 5 G1 -50 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V\nV9 6L6GC: 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 455 V, 5 G1 -50 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V",
